{
  "schema": "open-mathematics-course/v1",
  "id": "LG-MF",
  "title": "Modular forms",
  "description": "A working nineteen-lesson course on modular forms built from the geometry of the upper half-plane. It develops modular curves, holomorphic forms, Hecke operators and newforms, L-functions, theta series, cohomology and modular symbols, complex elliptic curves, non-holomorphic Eisenstein series and the Rankin–Selberg method. The lessons include written proofs, computed examples, exercises and solutions, and identify the required proofs and dependencies that remain unfinished.",
